These follow up "[PATCH v2 00/16] Move beastie and lab-claude onto
lab-mail" [1], after Pat's report in its thread that mbsync dumped
core on beastie when the local folders did not exist, and that
nothing says how to set up lab-claude [2].

Patch 1 has just install-mail on beastie make the list's four
folders, not just sent, so the first sync finds every folder it
expects.

Patch 2 keeps lab-claude's mbsync state inside each folder. By
default mbsync keeps it in ~/.local/state/isync, and lab-claude has
such state now, from a sync into a mail root that is gone. With it,
every sync into a new mail root fails with "Unable to recover from
UIDVALIDITY change", so the first real sync on lab-claude would have
failed. beastie keeps the default: Pat's sync there runs both ways
and already has state, and moving that state would make mbsync treat
the folders as new and copy each message to the other side.

Patch 3 documents lab-claude's setup in its README, from the configs
the jail installs to lab-process-mail, and has bootstrap.sh make the
list's folders too.

Tested: install-mail.sh in a scratch home makes all five folders and
leaves the password file alone on a second run. In a scratch home on
lab-claude, with the dist configs, the notmuch package, and the
folders from bootstrap.sh, mbsync pulls the list, notmuch new tags it,
and just check in dotfiles/notmuch passes every check. With patch 2,
removing the mail root and syncing again works. I could not reproduce
the core dump with isync 1.5.1 on lab-claude. There, missing folders
under an existing root are created, and a missing root gives "cannot
open store".

The series applies to Pat's patches 1-10 of v2 on b/dev. Patches
11-16 of v2 rebase onto it without conflicts.

